WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.200
Normally, we don't like to talk about youtube drama

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.980
but there's something going on right now that transcends that.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.500
As you may know,  h3h3 is being sued by

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.219
another youtuber because they used his

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.260
work in one of their videos.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.380
Now to everyone on this platform that seems

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:17.970
totally normal because the expectation

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.039
is when you put something on YouTube you

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.740
are putting it before a public forum and

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.280
if other people want to comment on that

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.800
material they have the right to do so,

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.220
So long as they add something and they keep it

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.920
creative and they generally give you credit.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.200
Now, that's a lot different than

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.239
the way that things used to be and the

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:38.940
crux of the issue here is that there's a

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.940
problem with copyright law and the way

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.620
that it was written and originally intended.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.240
Not only as a member of Corridor Digital

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.420
but as a lawyer in the state of California

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.100
I think it's super important that we take a moment to

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.720
examine not only what's before h3h3 here,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.500
but what it means for the rest of the platform and for the future of copyright law.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.940
There's a lot of assumptions about what fair use is

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:10.720
so let's clarify what it is and what it's not

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.260
The first thing to remember is that fair use

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.780
is not a right, it's a defence.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:16.760
In order to argue an

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.280
affirmative defense you must present it

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.070
to a fact-finder ie a judge or jury before the

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.930
court and only under the facts of your

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.080
particular case. Therefore, you must go

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.540
through a lengthy and costly court

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.270
process in order to assert this defense

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:34.910
and that's exactly why the h3 h3 case is

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.070
taking so long and costing so much money

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.509
when they have their day in court the

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:40.430
judge will look to four factors to

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.810
determine whether or not the various

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.910
defence applies. Number 1: He will look to

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.710
the purpose and character of the use.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.720
Now, this one is very important the

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.759
judge will be looking to see if whether

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:51.830
or not when h3h3 took the

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.539
video from the other youtuber and put it

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:55.850
in their own, they added something to

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.060
that youtuber's video. In this particular

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.380
case, they put three minutes of another

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.060
youtuber's video in between 11 minutes

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.100
of their own creative commentary but

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.200
they didn't actually touch or affect

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.420
the other youtubers work so it

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.920
ultimately comes down to the judge or

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.950
jury to decide whether or not placing

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:18.349
someone else's video in-between moments

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:20.660
of constructive creative comedic

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.180
commentary is in and of itself

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.940
transformative or if it's not because

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.760
they just took it and placed it and then

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.830
added stuff of their own separately.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.900
If h3h3 wins, it will set a

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.510
precedent that says their style of video

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:38.360
creating does fall under the first

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.040
factor of fair use. The second factor

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.360
that the judge will look at is the

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.099
nature of the copyrighted work itself

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:46.820
and whether or not that work is strongly copyrightable.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:49.280
Is it original? Is it unique?

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.080
The answer is yes and this factor

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.310
actually does fall in that other

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.440
youtubers favor. Number 3: the judge

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.120
will look to the amount and substantiality

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.160
of the portion used in relation to the

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.700
copyrighted work as a whole. Here, h3h3 used

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.270
the entire video which traditionally is

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.970
a bad thing but just like in the music

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.980
industry, where the courts had to come

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.140
up with a guideline so that musicians could

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.450
cover other musicians songs, the same

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.250
thing is happening here but the law

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.290
hasn't caught up yet. People online

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:20.990
considerate it entirely fair and normal to take

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.090
someone else's video and add something

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.400
to it. You look at the way that Mike Diva

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.590
has done dubstep remixes, you look at the way

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.480
that h3h3 has done comedic

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.340
commentary on other people's videos.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.220
This goes on across the board and

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.540
it's considered acceptable by the

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.150
community. But the law hasn't caught up yet

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.620
this is exactly where the problem lies.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.050
At number 4, the court will consider

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.660
the effect of the new use on the market

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.940
of the original copyrighted work.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:49.820
Does the new use add value or takeaway value

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.370
from the original copyright? In this case

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.530
I think h3h3's use definitely

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.540
adds value to the original youtuber's

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.330
video because it gets him more views it

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:02.209
gets his name out there and it overall

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:04.800
adds value to his channel across the platform.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.280
As you can see this case

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.620
ultimately comes down to two things

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.600
whether or not the court will consider h3h3's

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.230
use to be transformative and

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.610
whether or not they will consider the

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:14.540
type of use

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:15.950
that's being made across the digital

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.950
community to be fair much in the same

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.229
way that they had to recognize musicians

00:04:21.229 --> 00:04:23.380
making covers of other people's songs

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.920
the problem is they haven't quite caught

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:30.080
up with this yet, and if h3h3 is able to win

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.390
this case on this fair use defense, it

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:34.820
will set precedent for the rest of the

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.680
digital space and the rest of our

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.750
community and this is what makes this

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.340
case super super important.

